Top 50 DevOps interview questions from Tech Mahindra with real time scenarios 

1) Linux
How do you check CPU, memory, and disk utilization on a Linux server?
What is the difference between top, ps, and htop?
How do you find which process is listening on a particular port?
How would you troubleshoot a Linux server with 100% CPU utilization?
What is the difference between a hard link and a symbolic link?
How do you schedule a cron job to run every 15 minutes?

2) Git
What is the difference between git fetch, git pull, and git clone?
How do you resolve a Git merge conflict?
What is git stash, and when would you use it?
What is the difference between git merge and git rebase?
What happens if someone accidentally commits a password to Git?
How would you revert a bad production commit?

3) Docker
What is the difference between a Docker image and a container?
What is the difference between CMD and ENTRYPOINT?
What is the purpose of a Dockerfile?
How do you persist container data after a container is deleted?
How do you check the logs of a running container?
A Docker container keeps restarting. How would you troubleshoot it?

4) Jenkins / CI-CD
Explain a CI/CD pipeline you have worked on.
What is a Jenkinsfile?
What is the difference between declarative and scripted Jenkins pipelines?
How do you securely store passwords/tokens in Jenkins?
A Jenkins deployment failed halfway through. What would you do?
How would you implement rollback in a CI/CD pipeline?

5) AWS
What is the difference between EC2, ECS, EKS, and Lambda?
What is the difference between S3, EBS, and EFS?
What is the difference between a Security Group and a NACL?
What is the difference between an IAM user, role, and policy?
An EC2 instance is running but SSH isn't working. How would you troubleshoot it?
How would you design a highly available application across multiple Availability Zones?

6) Kubernetes
What is the difference between a Pod, Deployment, and Service?
What is the difference between Deployment and StatefulSet?
What is a DaemonSet, and where would you use one?
What are ConfigMaps and Secrets?
Explain Kubernetes liveness and readiness probes.
What are taints and tolerations?
A pod shows CrashLoopBackOff. How would you troubleshoot it?
A pod is Pending for 20 minutes. What would you check?

7) Scenario questions — very important
Your application was working yesterday but suddenly users are getting 503 errors. Walk me through your troubleshooting process.
CPU usage on one production server reaches 95%. What do you check first?
A deployment succeeds in Jenkins but the new version isn't accessible. How would you troubleshoot it?
Your Kubernetes application works internally but cannot be accessed from the internet. What would you check?
Developers say, "It works on my machine, but fails in Docker." How would you investigate? 
